Track 1: Ballast Strangles the Whistle
- Story & Context: During the zero-visibility freeze of 1984 at Europoort, night-clerk Pieter wedged a rusty wrench into the dock siren after an unmanifested 400-meter freighter blew its dual air-horns directly against the concrete quay wall. The concussive blast of diesel exhaust and vibrating steel rattled the salt-crusted office windows until the glass splintered inward, drowning his LinnDrum cassette deck in freezing harbor spray. Instead of evacuating, Pieter cranked the master gain into the megaphone PA to return the vessel's low B-flat bellow, screaming "count your deadweight by the blind bell" into the grey void until the radar showed the ship had answered twice and vanished.
